    <title>Cobb salad with mango and lime dressing</title>
    <updated>2026-05-31T16:55:27.398690+00:00</updated>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1 style="text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;"&gt;Cobb salad with mango and lime dressing&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;br&gt;
        &lt;img src="https://www.strangerfoods.org/images/cobb-salad-with-mango-and-lime-dressing.webp" style="text-align:center;"/&gt;
        &lt;br&gt;
        &lt;p style="font-family:sans-serif;&gt;Cobb salads slide easily into the OTK ethos, as they’re all about using up what you have to create something playful and vibrant. Here we invite you to the Cobb salad playground, using this recipe as a baseline. Dig through your cupboards, rummage through your fridge and freezer, use what you can and what you have, and then build from there – all the while keeping the spirit of abundance and fun.&lt;/p&gt;</content>
